    "lesson": {
      "title": "Monopoly pricing and deadweight loss",
      "instruction": "Set the market demand intercept and base marginal cost. Observe where Marginal Revenue intersects Marginal Cost (MR = MC) to determine monopoly price and output.",
      "explanation": "Because a monopolist must lower the price on all units to sell more, its Marginal Revenue curve lies below Demand and has twice the slope. Setting MR = MC restricts output below the competitive level (P = MC), generating mark-up profit (shaded green) and social deadweight loss (shaded red)."
    },
